course: dictionary
lesson: 13367
title: Hashtag
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hashtag is a word or phrase with the # sign in front of it, used on social media. «Let's share our reading with #worldbookday» means: put this topic in a tag so everyone posting about it can find it. Tap a hashtag and you see all the posts that use it.
explain: The # sign is the symbol. People also call it hash, pound sign (in the US) or number sign. Hashtags have no spaces, so write #readingchallenge, not #reading challenge. Always check with a grown-up before you post, and keep personal details, like your address, out of your hashtags.
explain: Hashtag can also be a verb: people hashtag their posts. As a joke, someone might say «hashtag winning» out loud to sound trendy. That is just silly talk, not a real tag.
fact: A hashtag is a word or phrase with the # sign in front of it.
fact: «#worldbookday» helps people find every post about World Book Day.
fact: Hashtags have no spaces: «#bookclub» works, but «#book club» does not.
fact: The # sign is also called hash, pound sign or number sign.
fact: As a joke, you can say «hashtag» before a phrase to sound trendy, as in «hashtag winning».
exercise: «She added #bookclub to her post so her friends could find it.» What does the hashtag do? | It makes the post louder | *It groups posts about the same topic | It sends a message to her teacher | It deletes the post
exercise: Which hashtag is written correctly? | *#blackcat | #black/cat | black cat | #black cat
exercise: In the US, the # sign is often called what? | A full stop | A question mark | A hyphen | *A pound sign
test:
«Sam used #wildlife in his post about the rare owl.» Why did Sam use this hashtag? | *So people looking for wildlife posts could find it | So the owl would fly away | To delete his post | To say he is sad
test:
Someone says «hashtag winning» as a joke. What does this show? | *They are being silly and trying to sound trendy | A real prize has been won | A new school rule about hashtags | A message from the teacher
exam:
Which sentence uses hashtags correctly and safely? | Post your home address as a hashtag: #Lane12 | *Ask a grown-up before you post, then add #schoolgarden to your photo | Use #school garden with a space in it | Put a stranger's phone number in your hashtags
